# 1) Enterprise problem definition (the actual pain)
Secondary loan trades delay/fail because **procedural prerequisites** are unclear and repeatedly re-done:

- Transferability rules differ (assignment vs novation, eligible transferee, restricted lists)
- Consent thresholds vary (agent/borrower/majority/all-lenders)
- Notices required and timed (before/after effective date)
- Conditions precedent (KYC/AML, sanctions, forms) differ per deal
- Evidence of diligence is not systematized, so disputes are expensive

**Who suffers**
- Trading desk ops (settlement cycle)
- Loan agency teams (consents/notices)
- Buyer ops (DD packs)
- Legal (disputes)
- Risk (unexpected blockers)

**What “enterprise” means here**
- Deterministic decisioning (not AI)
- Explainability with clause trace
- Auditable evidence chain
- State machine for consents/notices
- Event-driven re-evaluation
- Integrations (venues/agents), idempotency, retries
- Full test harness

