# 5) Kernel services (full list + key code skeletons)

## 5.1 Obligation Scheduler (due/overdue)
Purpose: enforce dates and grace periods.

```java
@Service
public class EsgObligationScheduler {
  private final EsgObligationRepo repo;
  private final AuditService audit;
  private final Clock clock;

  @Scheduled(cron="0 0 2 * * *")
  public void tick() {
    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now(clock);
    for (var o : repo.findActive()) {
      if ("ACTIVE".equals(o.status)) {
        if (today.isEqual(o.dueDate)) {
          o.status = "DUE";
          repo.save(o);
          audit.record("ESG_OBLIGATION_DUE", "SYSTEM", o.obligationId, oToJson(o));
        } else if (today.isAfter(o.dueDate.plusDays(o.graceDays == null ? 0 : o.graceDays))) {
          o.status = "OVERDUE";
          repo.save(o);
          audit.record("ESG_OBLIGATION_OVERDUE", "SYSTEM", o.obligationId, oToJson(o));
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 5.2 Submission Service (immutable capture)
```java
@Service
public class EsgSubmissionService {
  public UUID submit(EsgSubmission sub, UserContext ctx) {
    ctx.require("BORROWER_USER");
    sub.submissionId = UUID.randomUUID();
    sub.status = "SUBMITTED";
    sub.submittedAt = Instant.now();
    repo.save(sub);
    audit.record("ESG_SUBMISSION_SUBMITTED", ctx.userId(), sub.submissionId, toJson(sub));
    events.publish(new DomainEvent("ESG_SUBMISSION_RECEIVED", sub.loanId));
    return sub.submissionId;
  }
}
```

## 5.3 Validation Service (range + unit sanity)
- Check value ranges (no negatives unless permitted)
- Check periodEnd not future
- Check metric exists for loan
- Check obligation matches metric
- Set `VALIDATED` or `REJECTED`

## 5.4 Evidence Store Service (hash + metadata)
- Upload file
- Compute SHA256
- Store metadata row
- Return `evidenceRef = sha256` (or evidenceId)

## 5.5 Verification Workflow (separate authority)
```java
@Service
public class EsgVerificationService {
  public void verify(UUID submissionId, VerificationRequest req, UserContext ctx) {
    ctx.require("ESG_VERIFIER");
    // attach assurance report hash, mark VERIFIED
    audit.record("ESG_SUBMISSION_VERIFIED", ctx.userId(), submissionId, toJson(req));
    events.publish(new DomainEvent("ESG_SUBMISSION_VERIFIED", submissionLoanId(submissionId)));
  }
}
```

## 5.6 Assurance Policy Engine (gating incentives)
Purpose: only apply margin changes if required assurance present.

Rule:
- If target consequence is INCENTIVE/PENALTY and policy requires THIRD_PARTY/AUDITOR then submission must have verification meeting it.

## 5.7 Target Evaluation Engine (deterministic)
- Find latest VALIDATED (and if required: VERIFIED) submission for metric within target window
- Evaluate comparator
- Write `EsgEvaluation` row
- Update obligation status MET/FAILED
- Emit events `ESG_TARGET_MET/FAILED`

## 5.8 Incentive Engine (bps delta)
- Map evaluation to incentive rule (delta_if_met, delta_if_failed)
- Create adjustment record status `EVALUATED`

## 5.9 Approval Engine (SoD)
- Only CREDIT_ADMIN can approve adjustments
- Must include reason code
- Audit event required

## 5.10 Posting Engine (integration-safe)
- Post to “Pricing Ledger” adapter (stub for hackathon)
- Store `postedRef`
- Mark status POSTED
- Emit event `ESG_INCENTIVE_POSTED`

## 5.11 Evidence Pack Builder + Hash Chain
- Assemble full pack as JSON
- Hash SHA256
- Link prevHash (per loan)
- Store pack row
- Audit export event

## 5.12 Replay Engine (as-of truth)
- Recompute state as-of date using append-only/time-versioned queries
- Must produce same outcomes as historical evidence pack

