## 16) LENDER ROLL & WEIGHTED CONSENT (REAL WORLD, NOT COUNTS)

### Why this matters
“Majority consent” is **almost never headcount-based**.  
It is **commitment-weighted** (by drawn/undrawn exposure).

### LenderRoll Model
```java
@Entity @Table(name="lender_roll")
public class LenderRollEntity {
  @Id public UUID id;
  public UUID loanId;
  public UUID lenderId;
  public BigDecimal commitment;   // total commitment
  public BigDecimal outstanding;  // current drawn
  public boolean votingEligible;
}
```

### ConsentWeightingStrategy
```java
public interface ConsentWeightingStrategy {
  int calculatePercent(List<LenderRollEntity> roll,
                       Set<UUID> consentedLenders);
}
```

### Commitment-Weighted Implementation
```java
@Component
public class CommitmentWeightedStrategy implements ConsentWeightingStrategy {

  @Override
  public int calculatePercent(List<LenderRollEntity> roll,
                              Set<UUID> consented) {

    BigDecimal total = roll.stream()
      .filter(LenderRollEntity::votingEligible)
      .map(r -> r.commitment)
      .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);

    BigDecimal consentedAmt = roll.stream()
      .filter(r -> consented.contains(r.lenderId))
      .map(r -> r.commitment)
      .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);

    if (total.signum() == 0) return 0;
    return consentedAmt.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(100))
      .divide(total, RoundingMode.FLOOR)
      .intValue();
  }
}
```

### Consent Engine (weighted)
```java
int pct = weightingStrategy.calculatePercent(roll, receivedLenders);
return pct >= rule.thresholdPercent
  ? Assessment.ok("Weighted majority met: "+pct+"%", rule.sourceClauseRef)
  : Assessment.required("Weighted majority pending: "+pct+"%", rule.sourceClauseRef);
```

